Destructuring
Destructuring extracts values from objects and arrays into named variables.

Object destructuring:

const config = { host: "localhost", port: 3000, tls: false };

const { host, port } = config; // host = 'localhost', port = 3000

// rename while destructuring
const { host: serverHost } = config; // serverHost = 'localhost'

// default values (used when the key is absent)
const { timeout = 5000 } = config; // timeout = 5000
Array destructuring:

const [first, second, ...rest] = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50];
// first = 10, second = 20, rest = [30, 40, 50]

const [, second] = [10, 20, 30]; // skip first element
In function parameters:

const greet = ({ name, greeting = "Hello" }) => `${greeting}, ${name}!`;

greet({ name: "Alice" }); // 'Hello, Alice!'
greet({ name: "Bob", greeting: "Hi" }); // 'Hi, Bob!'
