Spread and Rest
Spread expands an iterable into individual elements. Rest collects remaining elements into an array. Both use ....

// spread an array into function arguments
const nums = [1, 2, 3];
Math.max(...nums); // 3

// copy and extend an array
const a = [1, 2];
const b = [...a, 3, 4]; // [1, 2, 3, 4]

// rest parameters — collect extra arguments
const sum = (first, ...others) => others.reduce((acc, n) => acc + n, first);
sum(1, 2, 3, 4); // 10
